      "stdout": "Change an audio segment playback speed.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type; must match this typed shortcut\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --speed TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Playback speed, e.g. 2.0 or 1.2x. Canonical unit: x; bare\r\n                              absolute values remain accepted and Nx means relative\r\n                              multiplication. Range after normalization: (0,+inf].\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Constant 2x playback speed\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio speed --seg-id <UUID> --speed 2.0\r\n  # Relative multiplier form (1.2x of current speed)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio speed --seg-id <UUID> --speed 